%N A402507 Least number congruent to 7 modulo 8 that is a quadratic residue modulo the first n odd primes.
%C A402507 Let N = A102476(n+2) be the least modulus with 2^(n+2) square roots of 1. a(n) is the minimal element of the coset of (Z/NZ)*^2 in (Z/NZ)* containing A402502(n+1) = (N/4 + 1 or 3*N/4 + 1) == 7 (mod 8), or the least m coprime to N such that A402502(n+1)/m is a square modulo N. Here (Z/NZ)* is the multiplicative group of integers modulo N and (Z/NZ)*^2 is the subgroup of squares.
%C A402507 For each n, while a(n) is a square in R and in Q_p for 3 <= p <= prime(n+1), Q_2 is a witness of a(n) being a nonsquare (i.e., a(n) is not a (local) square in Q_2). Sequences -A045535, A401305, A401356, and A402547 are similar constructions (see A401305).
%C A402507 For any fundamental discriminant D of a quadratic field dividing N, kronecker(D,a(n)) = -1 if and only if D == 4 (mod 8) or D == 24 (mod 32).
%e A402507 The cosets of (Z/NZ)*^2 in (Z/NZ)* containing A402502(n+1), with N = A102476(n+2) for n=0..4:
%e A402507   {7}
%e A402507   {7}
%e A402507   {31, 79}
%e A402507   {79, 151, 319, 631, 751, 799}
%e A402507   {631, 751, 991, 1159, 1831, 2311, 2479, 2599, 2671, 2839, 3151, 3271, 3679, 3991, 4159, 4519, 4951, 4999, 5119, 5791, 5839, 6031, 6631, 6799, 7351, 7639, 7879, 8479, 8551, 9199}
%o A402507 (PARI) a(n) = A401305(n, 7) \\ see A401305 for its program; st == 7 (mod 8) allows to calculate a(n) if a(n-1) is known
%Y A402507 Cf. A102476, A402502.
%Y A402507 See A402499 for a list of related sequences.
%K A402507 nonn,new
%O A402507 0,1
